diff --git a/docs/changelog.md b/docs/changelog.md
index 95360753..8944ca2b 100644
--- a/docs/changelog.md
+++ b/docs/changelog.md
@@ -11,6 +11,13 @@
   - Cover Flow: under Classic and Classic Modern, an album turns over to its songs from the moment you press Centre and slows into place, and Return turns it back the same way. The turn hardly moved in its first frames.
   - Cover Flow: under Classic and Classic Modern, a playlist of up to 500 songs turns over to its songs, with their total time. Only playlists of up to 200 did; a longer one opened as a list, as it still does past 500.
   - User guide: it has a release of its own, [User Guide](https://github.com/DiamondBond/q2-pod/releases/tag/guide), as PDF, EPUB and Markdown, so a version's release carries only update.tar.
+  - EQ: holding **Playback** in Quick Settings opens **Headphones**, a list of your saved presets with the one playing marked. Picking one plays it at once and closes the list; with EQ per Output on, that output keeps it. **EQ Off** turns the EQ off, and **EQ Settings** opens the EQ page as the hold did before.
+  - Now Playing: **More Like This**, in Play/Pause's hold menu, plays up to 50 songs from your library by artists Last.fm finds similar to the playing song's artist, with a few by that artist, shuffled. It needs Wi-Fi and a Last.fm API key in `.scrobble.ini` (`[LASTFM]`, `API_KEY=`), but no Last.fm account.
+  - Library: **Listening Stats**, under Most Played, shows your time played and your 25 top artists, albums and songs for this week, this month, this year and all time. It counts the listens logged on the card for scrobbling, uploaded or not, so it works without an account.
+  - EQ: **Presets → Search OPRA** in Advanced finds your headphones in the OPRA database and saves one of their presets, as **Import from SD /EQ** does. Each preset shows who made it. The first time, **Download OPRA database** saves it to the card over Wi-Fi (about 13 MB); **Update OPRA database** gets the latest one. EQ data from OPRA, https://github.com/opra-project/OPRA, CC BY-SA 4.0.
+  - System: **Eject Card**, after System Update, makes the card safe to take out without shutting down. It stops playback and everything that writes to the card, then says "Safe to remove the card". A card still in use stays in, and the message names what holds it. Put a card back in and it is ready again by itself.
+  - AirPlay: while AirPlay plays, Play/Pause, the side buttons and a Bluetooth headset's keys reach a running card app that asks for them, such as a Roon app controlling the music it sends to the Q2. A headset's Play, Pause and Stop, an AirPod coming out or going back in, and a sleep timer play or pause that app instead of stopping AirPlay.
+  - AirPlay: while a card app such as a Roon app sends music to the Q2 over AirPlay, the Q2 shows its own Now Playing page with the cover, the title, artist and album, and a moving progress bar, in place of stock's AirPlay page.
 - **1.9.2**:
   - Now Playing: the heart fills or empties as soon as you choose **Add to Favourites** or **Remove from Favourites** on the hold menu. It kept its old look until the next song, so tapping it then undid the change.
   - Playback: **Previous** then **Next** comes back to the song you left after changing Shuffle, Repeat or Group by, or at the start of a new shuffled Repeat All round, and the songs not yet played still play. Next could jump past them, or stop the queue under Play All. **Previous Album** at those moments no longer skips the albums between.
@@ -99,13 +106,6 @@
   - Apps: a card app can show an icon in the status bar while it runs, and change it with its state, such as a VPN's icon, full while connected and greyed while not (`bar=`), where the bar has room for it beside the clock.
   - Books: the book reader is now an app from the App Store, not part of the firmware. Install it from **Library → App Store → Books**, then open it from **Library → Apps → Books**. It reads the same `Books` folder.
   - Wi-Fi transfer: while it is on, another website open in a browser on your network can no longer delete or add files on your card, or read them by pointing a name of its own at the Q2. The Q2 took any page's request as the transfer page's own, so an image or a form on another site could empty a folder. The transfer page now works only by the Q2's address in numbers, not by a name, and a script that changes the card with `curl` has to send that page as its `Referer` (`-e http://<address>:8888/`). A browser set never to send a `Referer` can still list and download, but not change the card.
